== campus | MORNING · FACULTY BUILDING | university faculty building entrance with stairs, trees and morning light | walkin
kemi (worried): Quddus, the deadline is in three days and I still need two recommendation letters.
quddus (wave): Three days? Kemi, lecturers are not printers.
kemi (shrug): I was going to ask the Head of Department. Big title, big letter, right?
quddus (think): Not always. A strong letter comes from someone who actually knows your work.
> 1f4e9 | WHO TO ASK | 1f9d1-200d-1f4bc Someone who taught or supervised you | 1f4c8 Who saw your results up close | 2b50 Not just the biggest title

== cafe | LATER · CAMPUS CAFÉ | busy campus café with a chalkboard menu and warm lights | cafe
kemi (think): So how do I ask?
quddus (talk): Ask at least three to four weeks before the deadline. And make their job easy: send your CV, your statement, the program, and the deadline.
> 1f4cb | SEND THEM A BRIEF | 1f4cb Your CV + transcript | 1f4dd Your statement of purpose | 23f0 Program + exact deadline | 1f4a1 2-3 things you did in their class
kemi (talk): And I should remind them what I did in their class?
quddus (thumbs): Yes. Your project, your grade, your research. Specific stories make strong letters.
kemi (cheer): Next time I'm asking one month early. With a brief. And chin chin.
